<title>JAPAN: Moody's rates Kyushu Electric eurobonds Aa1.</title>
<headline>Moody's rates Kyushu Electric eurobonds Aa1.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Moody's Investors Service said on Thursday it had assigned an Aa1 rating to Kyushu Electric Power Co Inc's $300 million 7.25 percent eurobond offering due 2007.</p>
<p>Moody's said in a statement that the rating is based on the company's importance to the local economy, its crucial role as a supplier within the Japanese utility industry and its very favourable industry operating environment.</p>
</text>
